hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19139","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, said: Bakr, meaning Ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, narrated to me, from Nabil, owner of the cloak, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Suhayb, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed, so I greeted, and he returned to me with a gesture. And he said: I know only that he said: With a gesture of his finger."
"19140","Hushaym informed us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, he said: A man of al-Namir ibn Qasit narrated to me, he said: I heard Suhayb ibn Sinan narrate, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man who promises a woman a dowry, while Allah knows he does not intend to pay it to her, deceiving her by Allah and rendering her private part lawful by falsehood, shall meet Allah on the day he meets Him as an adulterer. And any man who borrows a debt from a man, while Allah knows he does not intend to pay it to him, deceiving him by Allah and rendering his property lawful by falsehood, shall meet Allah the Almighty on the day he meets Him as a thief."
"19141","Waki narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to move his lips in the days of Hunayn with something he had not done before that. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet among those before you was charmed by his nation, saying: Nothing shall assail these. So Allah revealed to him to give them choice among one of three: either I set upon them an enemy from others who ravages them, or hunger, or death. He said: So they said: As for killing or hunger we have no strength for it, but death. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So seventy thousand died in three. He said: So he said: So I now say: O Allah, by You I strive, by You I assault, and by You I fight."
"19142","Bahz and Hajjaj said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I marvel at the affair of the believer. The affair of the believer is all good for him, and that is for none but the believer. If prosperity befalls him he thanks, and that is good for him. And if adversity befalls him he endures, and that is good for him."
"19143","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise they are called: O people of Paradise, you have an appointment with Allah you have not seen. So they say: What is it? Did You not whiten our faces and remove us from the Fire and admit us into Paradise? He said: So the veil is lifted and they look at Him. By Allah, Allah has not given them anything dearer to them than it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: For those who did good is the best and increase."
"19144","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire the Fire, they are called: O people of Paradise, you have with Allah an appointment. So they say: Did He not weight our scales and give us our books in our right hands and admit us into Paradise and save us from the Fire? So the veil is lifted. He said: So Allah the Almighty manifests Himself to them. He said: So Allah has not given them anything dearer to them than looking at Him."
"19145","He said: Affan narrated to us, from his book, he said: Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughira, narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed hummed something we did not understand, nor did he tell us of it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you perceive it of me? A speaker said: Yes. He said: I recalled a prophet of the prophets given troops of his people, saying: Who can match these, or who can stand to these, or a phrase like this. Sulayman doubted. He said: So Allah revealed to him: Choose for your people among one of three: either I set upon them an enemy from others, or hunger, or death. He said: So he consulted his people in that, and they said: You are Allah's prophet; we entrust that to you, so choose for us. He said: So he stood to his prayer. He said: And they used to resort, when they panicked, to prayer. He said: So he prayed. He said: As for an enemy from others, no; or hunger, no; but death. He said: So death was set upon them for three days, and seventy thousand of them died. So my hum which you see is that I say: O Allah, my Lord, by You I fight, by You I assault, and there is no might nor power save in Allah."
"19146","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us with this hadith exactly, with all this speech and with this chain, and he did not say in it: When they panicked they resorted to prayer."
"19147","Affan narrated to us, from his book: Sulayman narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I marvel at the affair of the believer. The affair of the believer is all good for him; that is for none but the believer. If prosperity befalls him he thanks, and it was good. And if adversity befalls him he endures, and it was good."
"19148","Affan narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the days of Hunayn moved his lips after the dawn prayer with something we had not seen him do. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, we see you do something you had not done; what is this with which you move your lips? He said: A prophet among those before you was charmed by the multitude of his nation, saying: Nothing shall assail these. So Allah revealed to him to give his nation choice among one of three: either We set upon them an enemy from others who ravages them, or hunger, or that I send death upon them. So he consulted them, and they said: As for the enemy we have no strength for them, and as for hunger we have no endurance for it, but death. So He sent death upon them, and seventy thousand of them died in three days. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I now say, when he saw their multitude: O Allah, by You I strive, by You I assault, and by You I fight."
"19149","Affan narrated to us: Hammad informed us: Thabit informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: For those who did good is the best and increase. He said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire the Fire, a caller calls: O people of Paradise, you have with Allah an appointment He wishes to fulfill to you. So they say: What is it? Did He not weight our scales and whiten our faces and admit us into Paradise and shield us from the Fire? He said: So the veil is lifted for them and they look at Him. He said: By Allah, He has not given them anything dearer to them than looking at Him, nor more delighting to their eyes."
"19150","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam informed us that Umar ibn al-Khattab said to Suhayb, may Allah be pleased with them: But for three traits in you there would be no harm in you. He said: What are they? By Allah, we do not see you fault anything. He said: Your kunya Abu Yahya while you have no child, your ascription to al-Namir ibn Qasit while you are a stammering man, and that you do not hold wealth. He said: As for my kunya Abu Yahya, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me it, so I shall not leave it until I meet him. And as for my ascription to al-Namir ibn Qasit, I am a man of them, but I was suckled at al-Ayla, and this stammer is from that. And as for wealth, do you see me spend but in right?"
